# Development and CI dependencies: the runtime packages plus tests, linting,
# cli.py, and pip-tools itself. -r pulls the runtime packages in; -c pins them
# (and anything shared) to the runtime lock, so dev and production match.
# Edit this file, then regenerate the lock file (see README.md, "Dependencies"):
#   pip-compile --strip-extras requirements-dev.in
-r requirements.in
-c requirements.txt
